    numericalExample: 'Two threads increment a shared counter 1,000,000 times each without synchronization. Each increment takes ~3 CPU cycles. Race window per increment: 1 cycle. Race probability per increment: ~0.33%. Expected race count: 0.0033 x 1,000,000 = 3,300 lost increments. Final counter value: between 1,000,000 and 2,000,000 (random). Expected value: ~1,996,700. Adding a mutex: each increment takes ~20 cycles (lock + unlock overhead). Total time: 40,000,000 cycles vs 6,000,000 cycles without locks. Correctness costs 6.7x more time.',
    metrics: ['Race detection rate (tools: ThreadSanitizer, Intel Inspector)', 'Deadlock frequency per 1000 executions', 'Lock contention time as percentage of total runtime', 'Critical section length (instructions or microseconds)', 'Priority inversion events in real-time systems'],
    optimizationPossibilities: 'Minimize critical section size, use lock-free data structures where possible, replace mutexes with atomic operations for simple counters, use read-write locks for read-heavy workloads, and detect races with dynamic analysis tools.',
